! "Gravitational Prestress Advection" through both solvers on one problem against one
! reference value: the restoring stiffness that arises when a body under its own
! weight is displaced vertically, so a column of material of density rho is advected
! through gravity. "GPA Coeff" is that rho*g. The only tests that used it before are
! the two elmer_earth_2d_2layer cases, which need a Maxwell material as well and so
! cannot say which of the two capabilities an answer came from; here it is alone.
!
! WHAT THE TEST IS REALLY FOR. The term is genuinely not symmetric: it couples the
! gradient of the vertical displacement to every test component, so its transpose is
! a different operator. StressSolveLegacy symmetrises its whole local stiffness
! before gluing it in, and since every other term it assembles is symmetric already,
! that blanket operation only ever changed this one -- silently halving it and adding
! its transpose. ElasticSolver assembles the term in full, which is the model; this
! test is what pins that, and the difference is loud here. The symmetric half gives
! 2.61E-01 against this 9.16E-02. On the earth cases the same difference is worth
! only 2.6%, which is why this case exists rather than relying on them.
!
! The sign is a check in its own right. Without the keyword at all the norm is
! 1.93E-01, so the full term STIFFENS the body -- a smaller displacement than no
! advection -- as a restoring force should, while the symmetric half softened it to
! 2.61E-01. If a future change makes this norm exceed 1.93E-01 the term has changed
! sign or lost half of itself again.
!
! The load is vertical, since a term coupling to the vertical displacement cannot be
! exercised by shear alone.

Header
  Mesh DB "." "square"
End

Simulation
  Max Output Level = 5
  Coordinate System = Cartesian 2D
  Simulation Type = Steady State
  Steady State Max Iterations = 1
End

Body 1
  Equation = 1
  Material = 1
  Body Force = 1
End

Material 1
  Density = Real 0
  Youngs Modulus = Real 1
  Poisson Ratio = Real 0.3
End

Body Force 1
  Stress BodyForce 2 = Real -0.1
  Gravitational Prestress Advection = Logical True
  GPA Coeff = Real 2.0
End

Equation 1
  Active Solvers(2) = 1 2
End

Solver 1
  Equation = "Stress Analysis"
  Procedure = "StressSolve" "StressSolver"
  Variable = String "sDisp[sDisp:2]"
  Displace Mesh = Logical False

  Linear System Solver = Direct
  Linear System Direct Method = UMFPACK

  Nonlinear System Max Iterations = 1
  Steady State Convergence Tolerance = 1.0e-8
End

Solver 2
  Equation = "Elasticity Analysis"
  Procedure = "ElasticSolve" "ElasticSolver"
  Variable = String "eDisp[eDisp:2]"
  Large Deflection = False
  Displace Mesh = Logical False

  Linear System Solver = Direct
  Linear System Direct Method = UMFPACK

  Nonlinear System Max Iterations = 20
  Nonlinear System Convergence Tolerance = 1.0e-9
  Steady State Convergence Tolerance = 1.0e-8
End

Boundary Condition 1
  Target Boundaries(1) = 1
  sDisp 1 = Real 0
  sDisp 2 = Real 0
  eDisp 1 = Real 0
  eDisp 2 = Real 0
End

Boundary Condition 2
  Target Boundaries(1) = 3
  Force 2 = Real -0.05
End

Solver 1 :: Reference Norm = Real 9.16218950E-02
Solver 2 :: Reference Norm = Real 9.16218950E-02
